# This file works as an allow-list, not a deny-list.
#
# The rule for this repository is that only what is needed to run the application and satisfy
# docs/prd/assessment-prd.md is tracked. A conventional .gitignore cannot express that, because it has
# to name every unwanted thing in advance and so lets the next stray file in by default. So the root is
# ignored outright and the few things that belong are added back by name.
#
# The consequence to know about: a new top-level file or directory is ignored until it is listed here.
# `git add` says so rather than failing quietly — it prints "The following paths are ignored" — but it
# is a real cost, and the reason for it is that "everything else is ignored" is otherwise unenforceable.
#
# Tracked, and why:
#   .gitignore                    this contract
#   README.md                     how to run and test the application
#   AGENTS.md                     agent skill pointers (issue tracker, triage labels, domain docs)
#   CONTEXT.md                    single-context domain reference cited by AGENTS.md
#   docs/prd/                     the PRD, which is the source of truth for behaviour
#   docs/decisions.md             the ten questions the PRD left open, and how each was settled.
#                                 Kept because the code cites it: without it, deliberate choices
#                                 (registration not auto-logging in, a 72-byte password ceiling) look
#                                 like oversights.
#   api/                          Spring Boot service, including the integration tests the PRD requires
#   web/                          React frontend, its build config, and its browser tests
#
# Deliberately not tracked: the agent-workflow scaffolding this project was built with — story tickets,
# dependency graphs, estimates, PM reports, skill documentation, orchestrator caches and the ad-hoc
# verification scripts. None of it is needed to build, run, test or understand the application.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ignore everything at the root, then allow back what belongs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*

!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/CONTEXT.md
!/api/
!/docs/
!/web/

# docs/ carries requirements only, not process notes.
/docs/*
!/docs/prd/
!/docs/decisions.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and dependencies inside the two packages.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
target/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test and tooling output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
coverage/
# Screenshots from the capture-theme utility: regenerable, and committed images go stale silently.
screenshots/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local environment and editor noise. Unanchored, so they apply at any depth.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
